weak|PASS: Physical strength and convincing support retain separate source ordinals. A bending branch and an explanation missing evidence are distinct examples; the weak explanation translation preserves the causal relationship.
disgraceful|PASS: The term expresses strong disapproval rather than a measured quality or legal verdict. Deliberate memorial damage is a fictional reported evaluation; Vietnamese đáng hổ thẹn maintains that register.
heavy|PASS: Weight is separated from traffic amount/intensity. Heavier/heaviest spelling is correct; the chest and bus examples use different collocations and preserve location and consequence in Vietnamese.
mad|REVIEW: American anger and an informal judgement about an unreasonable idea are separated. The second avoids equating a clinical condition with foolishness; register and sensitive wording remain owner-review obligations.
orchestra|REVIEW: The instrumental ensemble boundary and qualified conductor claim are appropriate. The Vietnamese tuning example over-specifies strings and sound; replace it with cao độ in an additive field overlay and re-review the batch.
